# Normalise line endings in the repository, independent of the cloner's
# core.autocrlf setting.
#
# Why this file exists: this machine has the Git for Windows default
# `core.autocrlf=true`, which silently rewrote the working tree of every text
# file during the first `git add` (files nobody intended to touch). Declaring
# the rules here makes the same commit reproducible on any machine.
#
# `eol=lf` (not `text=auto`) is deliberate for the PowerShell scripts:
# install.ps1 / migrate.ps1 / verify.ps1 / test-migrate.ps1 are checked out as
# LF on every platform so their bytes are identical everywhere. That matters
# because PowerShell 5.1 decides how to decode a BOM-less .ps1 from its
# content and the console code page -- the scripts are kept pure ASCII so this
# is safe, and pinning the bytes keeps it that way.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.ps1   text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf

# Never touch binary content.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.zip   binary
*.exe   binary
